# 必考词 Unit28
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2025红宝书考研英语词汇
# 描述: 必考词Unit28核心词汇

{{plea}}{{/pliː}}{{n. 请求； plea；辩解}}{{He made a plea for more time.}}
{{plead}}{{/pliːd}}{{v. 恳求； plead；辩护}}{{He pleaded not guilty to the charges.}}
{{pledge}}{{/pledʒ}}{{n./v. 誓言； pledge；保证}}{{The government pledged to reduce emissions.}}
{{plunge}}{{/plʌndʒ}}{{v./n. 跳入； plunge；暴跌}}{{Stock prices plunged after the announcement.}}
{{poise}}{{/pɔɪz}}{{n./v. 沉着； poise；平衡}}{{She handled the situation with poise.}}
{{polar}}{{/ˈpəʊlər}}{{adj. 极地的； polar；截然相反的}}{{The two groups hold polar opposite views.}}
{{policy}}{{/ˈpɒləsi}}{{n. 政策； policy；方针}}{{The government introduced a new policy.}}
{{polish}}{{/ˈpɒlɪʃ}}{{v./n. 擦亮； polish；润色}}{{She polished her essay before submitting it.}}
{{poll}}{{/pəʊl}}{{n./v. 民意调查； poll；投票}}{{The latest poll shows a close race.}}
{{ponder}}{{/ˈpɒndər}}{{v. 沉思； ponder；考虑}}{{He pondered the question carefully.}}
{{popular}}{{/ˈpɒpjələr}}{{adj. 流行的； popular；受欢迎的}}{{The song became very popular.}}
{{portion}}{{/ˈpɔːʃn}}{{n. 部分； portion；一份}}{{A large portion of the budget goes to defense.}}
{{pose}}{{/pəʊz}}{{v./n. 摆姿势； pose；造成}}{{Pollution poses a threat to health.}}
{{postpone}}{{/pəˈspəʊn}}{{v. 推迟； postpone；延期}}{{The meeting was postponed until next week.}}
{{potential}}{{/pəˈtenʃl}}{{adj./n. 潜在的； potential；潜力}}{{The project has great potential.}}
{{precede}}{{/prɪˈsiːd}}{{v. 先于； precede；在…之前}}{{A brief introduction preceded the lecture.}}
{{precise}}{{/prɪˈsaɪs}}{{adj. 精确的； precise；准确的}}{{Can you give a more precise answer?}}
{{predict}}{{/prɪˈdɪkt}}{{v. 预测； predict；预言}}{{It is hard to predict the future.}}
{{prejudice}}{{/ˈpredʒudɪs}}{{n./v. 偏见； prejudice；损害}}{{Racial prejudice is a serious problem.}}
{{preliminary}}{{/prɪˈlɪmɪnəri}}{{adj./n. 初步的； preliminary；准备工作}}{{The preliminary results are promising.}}
{{premise}}{{/ˈpremɪs}}{{n. 前提； premise；房产}}{{The argument is based on a false premise.}}
{{premium}}{{/ˈpriːmiəm}}{{n./adj. 保险费； premium；优质的}}{{Customers pay a premium for quality.}}
{{prescribe}}{{/prɪˈskraɪb}}{{v. 开处方； prescribe；规定}}{{The doctor prescribed antibiotics.}}
{{preserve}}{{/prɪˈzɜːv}}{{v. 保存； preserve；保护}}{{We must preserve our cultural heritage.}}
{{prestige}}{{/preˈstiːʒ}}{{n. 威望； prestige；声望}}{{The university has great prestige.}}
{{presume}}{{/prɪˈzjuːm}}{{v. 假定； presume；冒昧}}{{I presume you have read the report.}}
{{prevail}}{{/prɪˈveɪl}}{{v. 盛行； prevail；获胜}}{{Common sense prevailed in the end.}}
{{prevent}}{{/prɪˈvent}}{{v. 阻止； prevent；预防}}{{The vaccine prevents the disease.}}
{{previous}}{{/ˈpriːviəs}}{{adj. 先前的； previous；以前的}}{{She had no previous experience.}}
{{primary}}{{/ˈpraɪməri}}{{adj. 主要的； primary；初级的}}{{Education is the primary concern.}}
{{prime}}{{/praɪm}}{{adj./n. 主要的； prime；全盛期}}{{He is in the prime of his career.}}
{{principal}}{{/ˈprɪnsəpl}}{{adj./n. 主要的； principal；校长}}{{The principal spoke at the ceremony.}}
{{principle}}{{/ˈprɪnsəpl}}{{n. 原则； principle；原理}}{{He is a man of principle.}}
{{prior}}{{/ˈpraɪər}}{{adj. 在先的； prior；更重要的}}{{Prior to the meeting, read the report.}}
{{priority}}{{/praɪˈɒrəti}}{{n. 优先事项； priority}}{{Safety is our top priority.}}
{{privilege}}{{/ˈprɪvəlɪdʒ}}{{n. 特权； privilege；荣幸}}{{Education is a right, not a privilege.}}
{{probe}}{{/prəʊb}}{{v./n. 探索； probe；调查}}{{The committee launched a probe into the matter.}}
{{proceed}}{{/prəˈsiːd}}{{v. 继续进行； proceed；前进}}{{Please proceed with the next item.}}
{{proclaim}}{{/prəˈkleɪm}}{{v. 宣布； proclaim；表明}}{{The president proclaimed a state of emergency.}}
{{productive}}{{/prəˈdʌktɪv}}{{adj. 高效的； productive；多产的}}{{It was a productive meeting.}}
{{profession}}{{/prəˈfeʃn}}{{n. 职业； profession}}{{She chose law as her profession.}}
{{profit}}{{/ˈprɒfɪt}}{{n./v. 利润； profit；获利}}{{The company made a large profit.}}
{{profound}}{{/prəˈfaʊnd}}{{adj. 深刻的； profound；渊博的}}{{The book had a profound impact.}}
{{prohibit}}{{/prəˈhɪbɪt}}{{v. 禁止； prohibit；阻止}}{{Smoking is prohibited indoors.}}
{{prominent}}{{/ˈprɒmɪnənt}}{{adj. 突出的； prominent；著名的}}{{He is a prominent figure in science.}}
{{promote}}{{/prəˈməʊt}}{{v. 促进； promote；晋升}}{{The campaign promotes healthy eating.}}
{{prompt}}{{/prɒmpt}}{{adj./v. 迅速的； prompt；促使}}{{The incident prompted a review.}}
{{prone}}{{/prəʊn}}{{adj. 易于的； prone；俯卧的}}{{Children are prone to infections.}}
{{propaganda}}{{/ˌprɒpəˈɡændə}}{{n. 宣传； propaganda}}{{The government used propaganda to influence opinion.}}
{{propel}}{{/prəˈpel}}{{v. 推动； propel；驱使}}{{Technology propelled economic growth.}}
{{proportion}}{{/prəˈpɔːʃn}}{{n. 比例； proportion；部分}}{{A large proportion of the budget is for education.}}
{{proposal}}{{/prəˈpəʊzl}}{{n. 提议； proposal；求婚}}{{The committee approved the proposal.}}
{{propose}}{{/prəˈpəʊz}}{{v. 提议； propose；打算}}{{She proposed a new strategy.}}
{{prosecute}}{{/ˈprɒsɪkjuːt}}{{v. 起诉； prosecute；检举}}{{The company was prosecuted for fraud.}}
{{prospect}}{{/ˈprɒspekt}}{{n. 前景； prospect；可能性}}{{The prospects for growth are good.}}
{{prosper}}{{/ˈprɒspər}}{{v. 繁荣； prosper；兴旺}}{{The business has prospered recently.}}
{{protocol}}{{/ˈprəʊtəkɒl}}{{n. 协议； protocol；礼仪}}{{All staff must follow the safety protocol.}}
{{provision}}{{/prəˈvɪʒn}}{{n. 提供； provision；条款}}{{The provision of clean water is essential.}}
{{provoke}}{{/prəˈvəʊk}}{{v. 激怒； provoke；引起}}{{His remarks provoked anger.}}
{{prudent}}{{/ˈpruːdnt}}{{adj. 谨慎的； prudent；明智的}}{{It would be prudent to wait.}}
{{pursue}}{{/pəˈsjuː}}{{v. 追求； pursue；从事}}{{She decided to pursue a career in law.}}
{{qualify}}{{/ˈkwɒlɪfaɪ}}{{v. 使合格； qualify；取得资格}}{{He qualified as an engineer last year.}}
{{quote}}{{/kwəʊt}}{{v./n. 引用； quote；报价}}{{She quoted a famous philosopher.}}
{{radical}}{{/ˈrædɪkl}}{{adj./n. 激进的； radical；根本的}}{{The government proposed radical reforms.}}
{{random}}{{/ˈrændəm}}{{adj. 随机的； random}}{{The sample was selected at random.}}
{{range}}{{/reɪndʒ}}{{n./v. 范围； range；变化}}{{The hotel offers a wide range of services.}}
{{rank}}{{/ræŋk}}{{n./v. 等级； rank；排名}}{{The university ranks among the best.}}
{{rational}}{{/ˈræʃənl}}{{adj. 理性的； rational；合理的}}{{We need a rational approach.}}
{{raw}}{{/rɔː}}{{adj. 生的； raw；未加工的}}{{The data is still in raw form.}}
{{react}}{{/riˈækt}}{{v. 反应； react；起化学反应}}{{How did you react to the news?}}
{{realm}}{{/relm}}{{n. 领域； realm；王国}}{{He made contributions to the realm of science.}}
{{reasonable}}{{/ˈriːznəbl}}{{adj. 合理的； reasonable；公道的}}{{The prices are very reasonable.}}
{{rebel}}{{/rɪˈbel}}{{v./n. 反叛； rebel；叛乱者}}{{The soldiers rebelled against their commander.}}
{{recall}}{{/rɪˈkɔːl}}{{v. 回忆； recall；召回}}{{I can't recall his name.}}
{{recession}}{{/rɪˈseʃn}}{{n. 衰退； recession；萧条}}{{The economy went into a recession.}}
{{recognize}}{{/ˈrekəɡnaɪz}}{{v. 认出； recognize；承认}}{{I recognized him immediately.}}
{{recommend}}{{/ˌrekəˈmend}}{{v. 推荐； recommend；建议}}{{I recommend this book to everyone.}}
{{reconcile}}{{/ˈrekənsaɪl}}{{v. 调和； reconcile；和解}}{{They reconciled their differences.}}
{{recover}}{{/rɪˈkʌvər}}{{v. 恢复； recover；收回}}{{The economy recovered after the crisis.}}
{{recruit}}{{/rɪˈkruːt}}{{v./n. 招募； recruit；新成员}}{{The company is recruiting new staff.}}
{{reduce}}{{/rɪˈdjuːs}}{{v. 减少； reduce；降低}}{{We need to reduce waste.}}
{{refer}}{{/rɪˈfɜːr}}{{v. 提到； refer；参考}}{{Please refer to the handbook.}}
{{reflect}}{{/rɪˈflekt}}{{v. 反映； reflect；思考}}{{The results reflect the current situation.}}
{{reform}}{{/rɪˈfɔːm}}{{v./n. 改革； reform}}{{The government introduced reforms.}}
{{regime}}{{/reɪˈʒiːm}}{{n. 政权； regime；制度}}{{The regime was overthrown.}}
{{register}}{{/ˈredʒɪstər}}{{v./n. 登记； register；注册}}{{You need to register online.}}
{{regulate}}{{/ˈreɡjuleɪt}}{{v. 调节； regulate；管理}}{{The industry is strictly regulated.}}
{{reinforce}}{{/ˌriːɪnˈfɔːs}}{{v. 加强； reinforce；增援}}{{The evidence reinforces the theory.}}
{{reject}}{{/rɪˈdʒekt}}{{v. 拒绝； reject；驳回}}{{The proposal was rejected.}}
{{relate}}{{/rɪˈleɪt}}{{v. 与…有关； relate；叙述}}{{The article relates to current events.}}
{{release}}{{/rɪˈliːs}}{{v./n. 释放； release；发布}}{{The company released a new product.}}
{{relevant}}{{/ˈreləvənt}}{{adj. 相关的； relevant}}{{Please provide relevant information.}}
{{relieve}}{{/rɪˈliːv}}{{v. 缓解； relieve；解除}}{{The medicine relieved the pain.}}
{{reluctant}}{{/rɪˈlʌktənt}}{{adj. 不情愿的； reluctant}}{{She was reluctant to leave.}}
{{rely}}{{/rɪˈlaɪ}}{{v. 依赖； rely；信赖}}{{You can rely on me.}}
{{remain}}{{/rɪˈmeɪn}}{{v. 保持； remain；剩余}}{{The situation remains unchanged.}}
{{remedy}}{{/ˈremədi}}{{n./v. 补救措施； remedy；治疗}}{{There is no easy remedy for this.}}
{{remote}}{{/rɪˈməʊt}}{{adj. 遥远的； remote；偏僻的}}{{The village is in a remote area.}}
{{render}}{{/ˈrendər}}{{v. 使成为； render；提供}}{{The accident rendered him unconscious.}}
